# wc-web environment (Appendix D.1) — copy to .env.local for local dev.
# These are the host-overridable build-time vars (see README.md "Host integration").
#
# Auth mode XOR: exactly one identity path is active per build (prepareHeaders, §7).
#   demo  → standalone demo identity (X-Demo-Employee-Id), DEMO_AUTH_ENABLED gated server-side;
#           the demo header is attached by a standalone-only applier (absent from the remote build, REQ-I-008)
#   auth0 → OAuth2 / OIDC bearer-token path; the host injects getAccessToken() (the remote does NOT mint tokens)
# In the federated remote, the HOST owns this value; standalone uses it directly.
#
# ⚠️ Local standalone dev (`yarn dev`): you MUST copy this file to `.env.local`
# (gitignored) so Vite loads VITE_AUTH_MODE. Passing it inline
# (`VITE_AUTH_MODE=demo yarn dev`) does NOT reach `import.meta.env` → prepareHeaders
# throws `Unsupported VITE_AUTH_MODE` and every RTK Query hangs on a loading
# skeleton with no network request (ST.8d QA finding F1).
VITE_AUTH_MODE=demo
# auth0 alternative (hosted mode) — set instead of `demo` when embedded in the PA host:
# VITE_AUTH_MODE=auth0

# Base URL for the wc-api backend. Host-overridable. REQUIRED in production builds —
# resolveApiBaseUrl (src/app/baseApi.ts) fails fast at import if unset in a prod build
# rather than silently using a relative '/'. Dev/test fall back to '/'.
#
# ⚠️ Standalone MSW demo (VITE_AUTH_MODE=demo): LEAVE THIS UNSET. The mock Service
# Worker only intercepts SAME-ORIGIN requests, so the demo must use the relative
# base ('/'). Setting an absolute origin (e.g. http://localhost:8080) makes RTK
# Query fire cross-origin, bypassing the worker → the app hangs on a loading
# skeleton (9.15 Finding #2). Only set this when running the standalone against a
# REAL local backend (no mocks).
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
